{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Great Places to Visit"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Travel Guide"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Had Better, Ought To, and Might Want To for What is Advisable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might want</span> to to give advice. You can also use <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> to express a recommendation<br>You can use the contraction <span class=\"italic\">\u2018d better</span> when you speak."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> is a strong request or advice.</li>  <li><span class=\"italic\">Might want to</span> is a suggestion.</li>  <li><span class=\"italic\">Had better</span> can be used as a strong recommendation, or warning.</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You'd better pack warm clothes</span> = I strongly recommend that you pack warm clothes, otherwise you will be cold.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you love the winter and you enjoy untouched nature, you might want to envisage a trip to Antarctica.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you are thinking of visiting the South Pole, you ought to prepare for the harsh cold. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You'd better join the thousands of tourists who travel to Antarctica during the summer."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Would Rather for What is Preferable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the expression <span class=\"italic\">would rather \u2026 </span>+verb to express a preference.<br> You can also use the contraction <span class=\"italic\">\u2018d rather ... </li><br> You use <span class=\"italic\">Would you rather \u2026 ?</li> to ask about someone's preferences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Would rather \u2026</span> introduces a comparison between two options. You use this expression when the context clearly allows the subject to make a choice between one option or the other.</li>   <li>You use <span class=\"italic\">would rather</span> + than to express a comparison between two things.</li>   <li>When the subjects are different, you use <span class=\"italic\">would rather</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Past Simple</span>.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I would rather go to Antarctica in the summer than in the winter. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd rather enjoy Antarctica under less punishing conditions."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to envisage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to imagine the possibility of a future event"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: You might want to envisage a trip to Antarctica."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear about Antarctica."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fresh water"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "water that can be used for drinking or cooking "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The ice in Antarctica contains 90% of the world's fresh water supply."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to record "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to write down for further reference "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Scientists have recorded temperatures below -75 degrees Celsius."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob06aud03"}], "type": "targe